{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547410-bygones-and-sanctums","id":1547410,"title":"Bygones and Sanctums","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-31T22:46:25-08:00","id":1547410,"title":"Bygones and Sanctums","content":"We have Verbena character who has decided to rescue a small collection of Bygone cryptoflora from a dying Horizon Realm, which is not something I anticipated her doing. Does anyone recall there being an example or description anywhere suggesting whether Bygones can thrive within Sanctums built around a paradigm &quot;friendly&quot; to mythological lifeforms? I'm considering whether her greenhouse would be a viable long term solution, or else she may have to eventually find an appropriate Horizon Realm to take them in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T01:42:43-08:00","id":1547413,"title":"","content":"I see no reason why they should not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T02:04:23-08:00","id":1547414,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, bygones can live in a mage's sanctum without issue (see most edition's rules of custos and familiars). There are legendary bygones that are so out-of-touch with Consensus that a sanctum could only be a temporary measure, but much like mages pushing 500+ years old, these are rare exceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T07:00:02-08:00","id":1547418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547410-bygones-and-sanctums?p=1547414#post1547414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, bygones can live in a mage's sanctum without issue (see most edition's rules of custos and familiars). There are legendary bygones that are so out-of-touch with Consensus that a sanctum could only be a temporary measure, but much like mages pushing 500+ years old, these are rare exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I'd assumed as well. I could swear I'd seen something related to Sanctums as a habitat before, but it may have been in the Mage fiction rather than the game sourcebooks. Of the five she collected, one of them will probably have to be moved out into the wilds of some Horizon Realm anyhow, just because being plant mommy to a fern flower isn't the safest thing to be doing. Potentially useful to have around, but they attract malevolent spirits and ownership comes with a blessing/curse combination.<br /> <br /> Two of them could potentially spread or germinate, and I'm imagining they'd need a habitat with more quintessential oomph than a Sanctum in order for that to happen. She also rescued a pair of vampire pumpkins (hilariously, these were once a thing) which aren't subject to Paradox, and probably should not be encouraged to &quot;reproduce&quot; no matter how initially entertaining that could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T08:39:41-08:00","id":1547424,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that the nature of Sanctums should fit the Tradition, Craft or Convention in question. Verbena having a hidden grove for a sanctum makes perfect sense. Long before Shakespeare wrote the Tempest islands ruled by a wizard, witch, enchantress, whatever, were a thing. Mad Scientist with an island is a trope too. So, if the Bygones in question could survive on a small island or a hidden valley, Bygones in a sanctum should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T12:08:44-08:00","id":1547430,"title":"","content":"I apologize for the tangential question, but which supplements can I look up for Bygone Flora?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T17:12:28-08:00","id":1547438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547410-bygones-and-sanctums?p=1547430#post1547430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize for the tangential question, but which supplements can I look up for Bygone Flora?</div> </div> </div> </div>I spent some time earlier looking for exactly that, and so far as I could find Bygone flora is a totally neglected subject. I simply looked up examples of mythical flora for the characters to encounter, and discovered a few which presented problems they would have to deal with.<br /> <br /> I seriously hadn't considered that the characters might get it into their heads to preserve them, but in retrospect I should have. It was at that point it clicked in my head that those plants were Bygones by definition, and I then scrambled to figure out how to deal with them being removed from their doomed habitat.<br /> <br /> I've decided that the vampire pumpkins are likely the descendants of twisted experiments performed by some crazed Tzimisce, considering where and when that particular legend originated. I'm almost hoping she decides to put them in proximity of normal pumpkins, just so I can describe what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}